    "how_values_were_computed": "sp.css was parsed rule by rule and the CSS cascade was simulated for one element that carries class \"sp\" plus data-theme and data-material on the SAME element, with html carrying no attributes. That is how every artifact board applies them (e.g. <div class=\"sp app-root ambient\" data-theme=\"..\" data-material=\"..\" data-motion=\"..\">). :root rules therefore reach the element only by inheritance. var() references are resolved on the element where they are declared. \"resolved\" values are what that element computes; \"provenance\" names the winning rule.",
    "kept": "The six variants the web renders (Day and Night glass; their Reduce Transparency and High Contrast opaque sets), the type families and the scene asset facts. Fonts and the scene image are handled by the generator, not as plain tokens. Regenerate tokens.generated.css with: node apps/web/scripts/liquid-glass/gen-tokens.mjs"
